course: dictionary
lesson: 863
title: Big and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word big can mean different things, and the words around it show which meaning you need. Read the sentence, then ask: is this about size, about importance, or about age? «You can't get burnt when it's cloudy,» says your big sister: here big means older, because it describes a person in your family.
explain: «Sicily is the biggest island in the Mediterranean Sea.» Biggest means larger than all the others, so the clue is the whole group of islands. Bigger means larger than one other thing, so use it when you compare just two.
explain: Big can also mean important or serious. A big mistake is not a mistake that is large in size; it is a mistake that matters a lot. Try your meaning in the sentence: if it still makes sense, you have got it.
fact: Big means large in size or amount, as in «a big dog».
fact: Big also means important or serious, as in «a big day» or «a big mistake».
fact: Big means older when we talk about people in a family, as in «my big sister».
fact: Bigger means larger than another thing; biggest means larger than all the others.
fact: «Macaws are the biggest parrots», and the hyacinth macaw is about a metre long from beak to tail.
exercise: «Sicily is the biggest island in the Mediterranean Sea.» What does biggest mean here? | Oldest of all the islands | *Larger than all the other islands, not just one | Larger than all the other islands | Shortest of all the islands
exercise: What does big mean in «a big mistake»? | *Important or serious | Large in size, like a big dog | Older than the other mistakes | Loud and noisy
exercise: «Some hammerhead sharks gather in big schools near islands.» What does big mean in «big schools»? | Older | Important | *Large in amount | Sad and tired
test: Which word completes this? «Of all the parrots, the hyacinth macaw is the ___.» | bigs | bigger | *biggest | big
test: What does big mean in «a big day»? | Fast and busy | *Important or serious | Older | Large in size
exam: Jayden says big always means size. What is the right answer? | Yes, but only when talking about parrots | Yes, big always means size, so a big day is a day that is large | No, big never means anything about size | *No, big can mean size, importance or age, depending on the words around it
